[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-fb45a6f2-a2cc-4a8d-9f3d-6381c605bdba\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Papers</p><strong>Thu 15 Oct 2026 14:30 - 14:45 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/ase-2026/ase-2026-venue1-forum-2\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Forum 2</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track#program\" class=\"navigate\">Testing and Analysis: Static and Dynamic Analysis 2</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/ningyuhe\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Ningyu He</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"fb45a6f2-a2cc-4a8d-9f3d-6381c605bdba\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>Verifier-in-the-Loop LLM Solving of Heap Constraints for Concolic Execution</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>Concolic execution systematically explores program paths by solving symbolic constraints, but in object-oriented software its practical effectiveness is often limited by \\emph{heap constraints} over objects and heap structure, such as nullness, aliasing, runtime types, and field reachability. These constraints form a systematic bottleneck in real-world software because satisfying them requires constructing a concrete heap model rather than merely computing primitive valuations, which existing SMT-based concolic engines and symbolic heap techniques do not handle effectively. We present \\textsc{COHEC}, a hybrid concolic architecture that decomposes each target path condition into a primitive component solved by an SMT solver and a heap component handled by a \\emph{Heap Constraint Solver} (\\textsc{HCS}). Given extracted heap constraints, \\textsc{HCS} uses an LLM to propose candidate heap models and initialization code, while a trusted verifier executes and verifies the generated code, admitting only models whose initialization code constructs states that satisfy all constraints and keeping the LLM outside the trusted computing base. We implement \\textsc{COHEC} on top of JDart/JPF and evaluate it on 6{,}750 APIs from ten Java libraries, together with a stratified sample from \\texttt{commons-lang3} against the LLM-assisted baseline \\textsc{CONCOLLMIC}. The results show that \\textsc{COHEC} substantially improves path exploration and concrete valuation generation over native JDart, while achieving higher coverage than \\textsc{CONCOLLMIC} at lower time and token cost. Overall, the findings indicate that treating heap constraint solving as verified heap model construction is a practical and effective way to extend concolic execution to the object-sensitive behaviors pervasive in modern software.</p>\n<p></p><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1145/3832783.3834410\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"publication-link navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-link\"></span> DOI</a><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/shaoranxia\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Shaoran Xia<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Fudan University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/leyicheng\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Leyi Cheng<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Soochow University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/caihuadong\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Caihua Dong<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Fudan University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/dongdongshe2\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Dongdong She<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Hong Kong University of Science and Technology</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/bowang4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Bo Wang\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/bowang4/0bf39a31-4192-40ce-ade2-f12737f806b0/micro-avatar?1793538907000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Bo Wang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Beijing Jiaotong University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/xinpeng\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Xin Peng\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/xinpeng/ced72380-7f9b-4037-aaee-023286b679d2/micro-avatar?1793543764000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Xin Peng<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Fudan University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/zhendong1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Zhen Dong\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/zhendong1/66fcd07d-e170-4fa1-9662-6d826e0c2904/micro-avatar?1793771224000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Zhen Dong<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Fudan University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-le